IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rta-types`
IMPORT `rta-dates`

-- Residential Tenancies Act 1986 — GOAL 2: BONDS AND RENT.
--
--   "May the landlord require this bond, this rent in advance, or this rent
--    increase; by when must the bond be lodged and the receipt given; and
--    how much is the tenant liable for?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_1986_120.txt — ss 18-30,
-- 49A-49B, 56B, 66D.

§ `Goal 2 — bonds and rent`

§§ `Bonds (ss 18, 18AA, 18A)`

-- s 18 "(1) A landlord may require payment of a bond (a general bond) of no
-- more than 4 weeks' rent". s 18AA "(1) ... a pet bond of no more than 2
-- weeks' rent ... if— (a) the tenant is keeping, or intends to keep, a pet on
-- the premises; and (b) the landlord has agreed the pet may be kept on the
-- premises. (2) A landlord must not require payment of more than 1 pet bond at
-- any one time during a tenancy." s 18A "(1) A landlord may not require a
-- tenant to provide the landlord with any form of security".
@ref ss 18(1), (4), 18AA(1)-(2), (5), 18A
@export Whether a landlord may require a bond under ss 18, 18AA and 18A of the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 (NZ): a general bond of no more than 4 weeks' rent; a pet bond of no more than 2 weeks' rent, only if the tenant keeps or intends to keep a pet the landlord has agreed to, and only one at a time; and no other form of security. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN b IS A `Bond demand`  @desc The kind and amount of bond, the weekly rent, the pet facts, whether a pet bond is already held, and whether other security is required
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the landlord may require the bond` b IF
        NOT b's `other security required`
    AND CONSIDER b's `kind of bond`
        WHEN `a general bond` THEN
            b's `bond required` AT MOST 4 TIMES b's `weekly rent when the bond is required`
        WHEN `a pet bond` THEN
                b's `bond required` AT MOST 2 TIMES b's `weekly rent when the bond is required`
            AND b's `the tenant keeps or intends to keep a pet`
            AND b's `the landlord agreed the pet may be kept`
            AND NOT b's `a pet bond is already held`

-- s 18(2), 18AA(3): on a lawful rent increase, a further bond "not exceeding
-- the amount by which the rent payable for 4 weeks [2 weeks] has been
-- increased".
@ref ss 18(2), 18AA(3)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of bond`, old IS A NUMBER, new IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most further bond after a rent increase, kind` k `, weekly rent from` old `to` new MEANS
    max 0 (weeks TIMES (new MINUS old))
    WHERE
        weeks MEANS IF k EQUALS `a general bond` THEN 4 ELSE 2

§§ `Lodging a bond (ss 19, 66D)`

-- s 19 "(1)(b) the landlord shall, within 23 working days after the payment
-- is made, forward the amount received to the chief executive ... (1A)
-- Subsection (1) does not apply if a bond of 1 week's rent or less is paid in
-- respect of a boarding house tenancy. In that case, section 66D applies
-- instead." s 66D(1)(a) "the bond need not be lodged with the chief
-- executive".
@ref ss 19(1)(b), (1A), 66D(1)(a)
@export The last day a landlord may forward a bond to the chief executive under s 19 of the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 (NZ): the 23rd working day after it is paid; nothing for a boarding house bond of 1 week's rent or less, which need not be lodged (s 66D). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Bond payment`  @desc The day the bond was paid, whether it was paid under a boarding house tenancy, and its size in weeks of rent
      cal IS A `Local calendar`  @desc The Matariki Observance Days and local anniversary days
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day to lodge the bond, payment` p `, calendar` cal MEANS
    IF   p's `paid under a boarding house tenancy` AND p's `bond paid, in weeks of rent` AT MOST 1
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the` 23 `th working day after` (p's `bond paid on`) `, calendar` cal)

@ref s 19(1)(b), (2)
GIVEN p IS A `Bond payment`, cal IS A `Local calendar`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bond was lodged in time` p cal IF
    CONSIDER `the last day to lodge the bond, payment` p `, calendar` cal
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST last THEN
        CONSIDER p's `bond forwarded to the chief executive on`
        WHEN JUST sent THEN sent AT MOST last
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- s 22A "(3) The application may be made at any time after the termination
-- of the tenancy if party A is the tenant, but must be made within 2 months
-- of the termination of the tenancy if party A is the landlord."
@ref s 22A(3)
GIVEN who IS A `Who applies`, ended IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day for a bond application without agreement by` who `, tenancy ended` ended MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `a landlord` THEN JUST (`add months` ended 2)
    WHEN `a tenant` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `the chief executive` THEN NOTHING

§§ `Rent in advance and rent increases (ss 23, 24)`

-- s 23 "(1) A landlord shall not require the payment of any rent— (a) more
-- than 2 weeks in advance; or (b) before the expiry of the period for which
-- rent has been paid already. ... (3) A landlord shall not require any
-- payment of rent to be made by postdated cheque". (2) excepts a longer pay
-- period deduction under a service or employer tenancy.
@ref s 23
@export Whether a landlord may require rent in advance under s 23 of the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 (NZ): no more than 2 weeks in advance, not before the period already paid for has expired, and not by postdated cheque (the s 23(2) holiday pay deduction excepted). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN r IS A `Rent demand`  @desc The weeks of rent required in advance, whether it is required before the paid period ends, whether by postdated cheque, and whether the s 23(2) exception applies
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the landlord may require the rent in advance` r IF
        (   r's `weeks of rent required in advance` AT MOST 2
         OR r's `the s 23(2) longer pay period deduction applies`)
    AND NOT r's `required before the period already paid for expires`
    AND NOT r's `required by postdated cheque`

-- s 24(1) "(c) the day upon which the increased rent shall become payable
-- shall be not less than 60 days (or, in the case of a boarding house
-- tenancy, not less than 28 days) after the date on which that notice is
-- given". Counted under s 136A: the period starts the day after the notice
-- is given (or deemed given under s 136).
@ref s 24(1)(c), s 136A
GIVEN n IS A `Rent increase notice`
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest day the increase may take effect, notice` n MEANS
    `the last day of a period of` period `days after notice given on` (n's `notice given on`)
    WHERE
        period MEANS IF n's `a boarding house tenancy` THEN 28 ELSE 60

-- s 24(1) "(a) the landlord shall give the tenant notice in writing of the
-- increase; and (b) that notice shall specify the amount of the increased
-- rent and the day ...; and (c) [60 days, or 28] ...; and (d) the rent must
-- not be increased within 12 months after the date of the commencement of the
-- tenancy; and (e) the rent must not be increased within 12 months after the
-- date on which the last increase took effect; and (f) a landlord under a
-- fixed-term tenancy— (i) may not increase the rent during the term of the
-- tenancy unless permitted by the provisions of the tenancy agreement ...;
-- and (h) where the Tribunal has made an order under section 25 and that
-- order is still in force, the rent shall not be increased to an amount in
-- excess of the amount specified in the order." "Within 12 months after" a
-- date: a period "after" a day excludes it (Legislation Act 2019, s 54), so
-- the 12 months end on the anniversary and the increase may take effect only
-- from the day after it (fork F2; changed after the independent pass).
@ref s 24(1)
@export Whether a rent increase is lawful under s 24 of the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 (NZ): written notice stating the new rent and the day; that day at least 60 days (28 for a boarding house) after the notice is given; not within 12 months after the start of the tenancy or the last increase (the anniversary itself is within them); during a fixed term only if the agreement allows; and no higher than any market rent order in force. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN n IS A `Rent increase notice`  @desc The day the notice is given and the day the increase takes effect, the notice's content, the tenancy's start and last increase, whether it is fixed-term and the agreement allows increases, whether it is a boarding house tenancy, any market rent order, and the new rent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rent increase is lawful` n IF
        n's `notice in writing stating the amount and the day`
    AND takes AT LEAST `the earliest day the increase may take effect, notice` n
    AND takes GREATER THAN `add years` (n's `tenancy commenced on`) 1
    AND (CONSIDER n's `last increase took effect on`
         WHEN JUST last THEN takes GREATER THAN `add years` last 1
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE)
    AND ((NOT n's `a fixed-term tenancy`) OR n's `the agreement permits increases during the term`)
    AND (CONSIDER n's `market rent order amount in force`
         WHEN JUST cap THEN n's `new weekly rent` AT MOST cap
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE)
    WHERE
        takes MEANS n's `increase takes effect on`

§§ `Market rent (s 25)`

-- s 25 "(2) ... no application may be made under that subsection in respect
-- of the rent payable under a fixed-term tenancy later than 3 months after—
-- (a) the date of the commencement of the tenancy ...; or (b) the date of the
-- last review of rent,— whichever is the later. (2A) Despite subsection (2),
-- a tenant ... [of a unit title] may apply ... within 3 months after the
-- tenant ... becomes aware of a change in the body corporate operational
-- rules". A periodic tenant may apply "at any time".
@ref s 25(1)-(2A)
@export Whether a tenant may apply for a market rent order under s 25 of the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 (NZ): at any time under a periodic tenancy; under a fixed term, no later than 3 months after the later of its start and the last rent review, or 3 months after learning of a body corporate rule change that affects them. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN a IS A `Market rent application`  @desc The application date, whether the tenancy is fixed-term, its start and last rent review, and any body corporate rule change
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the market rent application is in time` a IF
        NOT a's `for a fixed-term tenancy`
    OR  made AT MOST `add months` from 3
    OR  (CONSIDER a's `aware of a body corporate rule change on`
         WHEN JUST aware THEN made AT MOST `add months` aware 3
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)
    WHERE
        made MEANS a's `market rent application made on`
        from MEANS
            CONSIDER a's `last rent review on`
            WHEN JUST r THEN IF r GREATER THAN a's `the fixed term commenced on` THEN r ELSE a's `the fixed term commenced on`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN a's `the fixed term commenced on`

-- s 25(5) "An order ... shall take effect on and from a date to be specified
-- in the order, which may be the date of the order or any earlier or later
-- date, but being no earlier than the date of the application for the order
-- and no later than 30 days after the date of the order."
@ref s 25(5)
GIVEN ordered IS A DATE, effective IS A DATE, applied IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a market rent order made on` ordered `may take effect on` effective `, applied for on` applied IF
        effective AT LEAST applied
    AND effective AT MOST `the day` 30 `days after` ordered

§§ `Receipts and records (ss 29, 30)`

-- s 29 "(2) The receipt shall be given to the person paying the rent— (a)
-- forthwith, where payment is made in cash; or (b) within 72 hours after
-- payment, in any other case." (4) none is needed for an automatic payment or
-- non-negotiable cheque from the tenant's account, payment into the
-- landlord's dedicated account, or a deduction from pay or benefit paid into
-- the landlord's account.
@ref s 29(1), (2), (4)
@export Whether the landlord met s 29 of the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 (NZ) on a receipt for rent: forthwith for cash, within 72 hours otherwise, and none needed for automatic payments or non-negotiable cheques from the tenant's account, payments into an account kept for the landlord's tenancies, or deductions from pay or benefit. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Rent payment`  @desc How the rent was paid, and whether and when a receipt was given
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the receipt rules were met` p IF
    CONSIDER p's `way rent is paid`
    WHEN `in cash` THEN p's `receipt given forthwith`
    WHEN `by another means needing a receipt` THEN
            p's `receipt given forthwith`
        OR  (CONSIDER p's `hours after payment the receipt was given`
             WHEN JUST h THEN h AT MOST 72
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 30 "(1A) The records must be kept for 7 tax years after the tax year to
-- which they relate. (1B) ... tax year means— (a) the period of 9 months
-- beginning with 1 July 2016 and ending with 31 March 2017; or (b) a later
-- period of 12 months beginning with 1 April and ending with 31 March." A
-- payment before 1 July 2016 falls in no tax year as defined.
@ref s 30(1A)-(1B)
@export The last day a landlord must keep the record of a rent or bond payment under s 30 of the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 (NZ): 31 March, 7 tax years after the end of the tax year (1 April to 31 March) of the payment. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN paid IS A DATE  @desc The day of the payment
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to keep the record of a payment on` paid MEANS
    IF   paid LESS THAN Date 1 7 2016
    THEN `s 30 defines no tax year before 1 July 2016`
    ELSE Date 31 3 (yearEnds PLUS 7)
    WHERE
        yearEnds MEANS IF DATE_MONTH paid AT LEAST 4 THEN DATE_YEAR paid PLUS 1 ELSE DATE_YEAR paid

`s 30 defines no tax year before 1 July 2016` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 30(1B) defines no tax year before 1 July 2016"

§§ `Damage (ss 49A, 49B)`

-- s 49A "Except as provided in section 49B, a tenant has no liability ... to—
-- (a) meet the cost of making good any destruction of, or damage to, the
-- premises". s 49B "(1) A tenant is not excused ... if ... (a) ...
-- intentionally ...; or (b) ... an imprisonable offence; or (c) ... keeping a
-- pet on the premises. (2) ... the tenant is liable ... for destruction of, or
-- damage to, the premises that is caused by a careless act or omission ...
-- (3) ... limited,— (a) if the property is insured ..., to the lesser of the
-- applicable excess under the insurance and ... [4 weeks' rent, or 4 weeks'
-- market rent for an income-related rent]; or (b) otherwise, to [4 weeks'
-- rent]. (4)(a) if any insurance moneys ... are irrecoverable because of an
-- act or omission of the tenant ..., the property is treated as not insured".
@ref ss 49A, 49B(1)-(4)
@export The tenant's liability for damage to the premises under ss 49A and 49B of the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 (NZ): the whole cost if intentional, an imprisonable offence, or caused by a pet; for careless damage, the cost up to the insurance excess or 4 weeks' rent, whichever is less (4 weeks' rent if uninsured or the insurance is lost through the tenant; market rent for an income-related rent); otherwise nothing. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN d IS A `Damage facts`  @desc How the damage was caused, its cost, the insurance and its excess, and the rent (or market rent for an income-related rent)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tenant's liability for the damage` d MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF d's `damage intentional, an imprisonable offence, or caused by a pet` THEN cost
        IF d's `damage caused by a careless act or omission` THEN min cost cap
        OTHERWISE 0
    WHERE
        cost MEANS d's `cost of making good the damage`
        fourWeeks MEANS
            4 TIMES (IF d's `the tenant pays an income-related rent`
                     THEN d's `weekly market rent under the Public and Community Housing Management Act`
                     ELSE d's `weekly rent under the agreement`)
        cap MEANS
            IF   d's `premises insured against the damage` AND NOT d's `insurance irrecoverable because of the tenant`
            THEN min (d's `insurance excess`) fourWeeks
            ELSE fourWeeks

§§ `Rent after a family violence withdrawal (s 56B(5)-(6))`

-- s 56B "(5) For the period of 2 weeks beginning with the day after the date
-- of the withdrawal, the rent payable for the premises is reduced to an
-- amount calculated in accordance with the following formula" (lost in the
-- conversion; its symbols are the rent otherwise payable, the tenants before
-- the withdrawal and the remaining tenants): read as rent × remaining ÷
-- before (fork F3). "(6) However, the amount of rent is not reduced ... if—
-- (a) ... income-related rent; or (b) [a prescribed PACHMA tenancy]; or (c)
-- [a prescribed tenancy or landlord]."
@ref s 56B(5)-(6)
@export The rent payable for the 2 weeks after a tenant withdraws for family violence under s 56B(5) of the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 (NZ): the rent otherwise payable times the remaining tenants divided by the tenants before the withdrawal (the Act's formula, lost in conversion, as read here), unless s 56B(6) excludes the reduction. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN rent IS A NUMBER  @desc The rent otherwise payable for the 2 weeks
      before IS A NUMBER  @desc The number of tenants immediately before the withdrawal
      remaining IS A NUMBER  @desc The number of remaining tenants
      excluded IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether s 56B(6) excludes the reduction (income-related rent or a prescribed tenancy)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rent for the 2 weeks after the withdrawal, rent` rent `, tenants before` before `, remaining` remaining `, excluded` excluded MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF remaining AT MOST 0 THEN `s 56B(2) ends the tenancy when no tenant remains`
        IF excluded THEN rent
        OTHERWISE rent TIMES remaining DIVIDED BY before

`s 56B(2) ends the tenancy when no tenant remains` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 56B(2): with no remaining tenant the tenancy terminates, so no rent is reduced"
